!! Show DIFF.md in a desktop window, re-rendering it whenever the file changes.
!!
!! Run with `allspeak diffshow`. This is a desktop application rather than a browser one, so the window comes from the Python runtime's graphics domain rather than from Webson.

!   diffshow.allspeak

    script Diffshow

!! @hash daa9b937
!!!

!! Load the desktop graphics domain, which supplies the window, the markdown panel and the Qt event loop this script is built on.

    use graphics


!! @hash 857a3262
!!!

!! Declare the widgets the script builds.
!!
!! Widget variables must exist before `create` can instantiate them. `mdpanel` is a read-only markdown panel — setting its text converts markdown to HTML and renders it, so DIFF.md reaches the screen as formatted prose rather than as raw source. It is created without `cols`/`rows` so that it expands to fill the window instead of being pinned to a character grid.

    window MainWindow
    layout Panel
    mdpanel DocPanel


!! @hash 3469f189
!!!

!! Declare the state shared between the startup path, the poller and the close handler.
!!
!! `Conf` is the saved geometry, `HaveGeometry` records whether a usable one was found, and `WinX`/`WinY`/`WinW`/`WinH` carry it to the `create` call. `Contents` is the text just read from DIFF.md and `Shown` is what the panel is currently displaying.

    dictionary Conf
    variable HaveGeometry
    variable WinX
    variable WinY
    variable WinW
    variable WinH
    variable Contents
    variable Shown


!! @hash 539cb056
!!!

!! Start from a known state before anything reads it.
!!
!! `reset` empties the dictionary and `clear` sets the boolean false — a flag must be initialised before it can be tested. Leaving `Shown` empty means the poller's first pass always renders, even if DIFF.md itself is empty.

    reset Conf
    clear HaveGeometry
    put empty into Shown


!! @hash 115fbaa1
!!!

!! Recover the window geometry saved by a previous run.
!!
!! Relative paths resolve against this script's own folder, so `` `.diffshow.conf` `` and `` `DIFF.md` `` are read from the project directory however the script is launched. On a first run the config file does not exist and the `on failure` clause leaves `HaveGeometry` false, so the script falls back to a default size and lets Qt centre the window.
!!
!! All four values are required: a truncated or hand-edited file is ignored rather than half-applied, which is why this is one four-way test instead of four reads of entries that might not be there.

    if file `.diffshow.conf` exists
    begin
        load Conf from `.diffshow.conf`
        on failure clear HaveGeometry
        if Conf has entry `x` and Conf has entry `y` and Conf has entry `width` and Conf has entry `height`
        begin
            put entry `x` of Conf into WinX
            put entry `y` of Conf into WinY
            put entry `width` of Conf into WinW
            put entry `height` of Conf into WinH
            set HaveGeometry
        end
    end


!! @hash 7f7216bb
!!!

!! Hand control to Qt.
!!
!! Everything after this point runs in slices on the runtime's flush timer rather than in one go, so the window becomes interactive while the rest of the setup is still finishing.

    init graphics


!! @hash d57326f7
!!!

!! Build the interface — layout, panel, window.
!!
!! The layout is populated before the window exists because `create … layout Panel` attaches it immediately. Only the window's geometry differs between runs, and it can only be set at `create` time, which is why the values recovered above are read here instead of applied afterwards.

    create Panel type QVBoxLayout
    create DocPanel
    add DocPanel to Panel

    if HaveGeometry
        create MainWindow title `DIFF.md` at WinX WinY size WinW WinH
    else
        create MainWindow title `DIFF.md` size 800 600

    set the layout of MainWindow to Panel


!! @hash 1e3e8dfb
!!!

!! Register the close handler while the window still exists to be closed.
!!
!! This is the last point at which the position can be read back, so the handler that saves it has to be in place before the window is shown.

    on close MainWindow go to SaveGeometry


!! @hash a5c47e1d
!!!

!! Show the window and start the watcher.
!!
!! The main flow ends at `stop`: the window and the poller are separate threads that keep running under the event loop, and the program exits when the last window closes.

    show MainWindow
    fork to PollDiff
    stop


!! @hash 61ea5ab9
!!!

!! Re-read DIFF.md once a second and re-render the panel only when the text has changed.
!!
!! The `wait` is what lets the rest of the program run between passes — a loop without it would starve the UI, since threads are cooperative and yield only at `wait`, blocking I/O or `stop`. The `file … exists` test keeps a missing file from raising an error every second; the panel says so instead.

PollDiff:
    if file `DIFF.md` exists
    begin
        load Contents from `DIFF.md`
        on failure put `DIFF.md could not be read.` into Contents
    end
    else
        put `No DIFF.md in ` cat cwd into Contents
    if Contents is not Shown
    begin
        set the text of DocPanel to Contents
        put Contents into Shown
    end
    wait 1 second
    go to PollDiff


!! @hash 1dfd4464
!!!

!! Save the window's size and position as the program shuts down.
!!
!! The handler runs inside the close event, before Qt destroys the window and before the runtime ends the program as its last window goes — so it runs straight through to `stop` with nothing in between that could yield. The JSON is written pretty-printed to keep the file readable by hand.

SaveGeometry:
    put the x of MainWindow into WinX
    put the y of MainWindow into WinY
    put the width of MainWindow into WinW
    put the height of MainWindow into WinH
    set entry `x` of Conf to WinX
    set entry `y` of Conf to WinY
    set entry `width` of Conf to WinW
    set entry `height` of Conf to WinH
    save prettify Conf to `.diffshow.conf`
    stop


!! @hash 44449fe7
!!!
